CAVEAT:  The case asks for traffic between 4 devices in opposite pairs. tb101 has one switch (the stack) and
         3 host links, so that part is NOT MEASURABLE here. This run used 2 routes in both directions instead:
         host bond0 <-> po1 <-> stack links <-> port3.0.1 <-> host eth2. The LACP partner is a Linux bond, not
         an AW+ switch. The port-down events used `shutdown` on the CLI, not a cable pull.
         Two observations are not graded as a FAIL, because the case's expected result held:
         O-1  At each member reload (E3, E4, E5), while the member joined again, 4 broadcast frames in one
              30 ms window reached the far side twice. Unicast frames were never duplicated.
         O-2  `show lacp-counter` shows "Pckt err Sent 2" on port1.0.1 after member 1 became master. The
              LACP state did not change, and port2.0.1 shows 0.
