STEP 3 -- "3. Conducted multiple port down events so that topology had to change totally"   PASS
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
  Method: 5 events, E1 to E5, each under traffic. During each event: l2flows at 100 pps per flow, and
  linerate A and B at 300 Mbps each way. 300 Mbps is a rate the host can receive without its own losses,
  so any loss measured is the DUT's or the event's. After each event, one 30 s window per direction at
  full rate. `show stack` was read before every event. Lines that start with "~" are recorded fields.

  | event | what                                   | master  | longest outage (l2flows)        | after: full rate A / B |
  | E1    | shutdown port1.0.1 (master's LAG link) | 1       | 380 ms toward DUT, 0 toward host | 100.0% / 100.0%        |
  | E2    | shutdown port2.0.1                     | 1       | 30 ms (no outage >= 50 ms)       | 100.0% / 100.0%        |
  | E3    | reload stack-member 1 (master + link)  | 1 -> 4  | 770 ms toward DUT, 80 ms back    | 100.0% / 100.0%        |
  | E4    | reload stack-member 2 (other link)     | 4       | 40 ms (no outage >= 50 ms)       | 100.0% / 100.0%        |
  | E5    | reload stack-member 4 (master, no link)| 4 -> 1  | 30 ms (no outage >= 50 ms)       | 100.0% / 100.0%        |
  After every event: po1 had 2 of 2 links synchronized, `show lacp sys-id` read 0000.cd37.0d6f, the host's
  partner MAC read 00:00:cd:37:0d:6f, and the MAC table was correct.

